# Extron SIS (Simple Instruction Set) Protocol Driver
#
# Controls Extron products over TCP (port 23) or RS-232 (9600 8N1).
# Covers 200+ products: crosspoint matrix switchers, presentation switchers,
# scalers, distribution amplifiers, and DSPs.
#
# Protocol reference: Extron SIS Command/Response Reference
# https://www.extron.com/article/sisseries
# (Matrix dialect verified against the DXP HD 4K PLUS user guide, 68-2939-01.
# The bulk views below are also in the XTP CrossPoint Series user guide,
# 68-1736-01 Rev. J, and the CrossPoint 450 Plus / CrossPoint Ultra / MAV Plus
# user guide, 68-521-20 Rev. F.)
#
# Command format: SIS commands execute as typed (no terminator); Esc-prefixed
# commands end with <CR>. Responses are terminated with CR+LF.
#
# The SIS family has two dialects this driver spans:
#
#   Single-output devices (scalers, presentation switchers, DAs):
#     {input}!           — Select input           -> "In{i} All"
#     {level}V           — Set volume             -> "Vol{level}"
#     1Z / 0Z / Z        — Mute / unmute / query  -> "Amt1" / "Amt0"
#     1B / 0B            — Video mute / unmute    -> "Vmt1" / "Vmt0"
#
#   Matrix switchers (DXP, CrossPoint, XTP):
#     {input}*{output}!  — Tie AV                 -> "Out{o} In{i} All"
#     {input}*{output}%  — Tie video only         -> "Out{o} In{i} Vid"
#     {input}*{output}$  — Tie audio only         -> "Out{o} In{i} Aud"
#     {input}*!          — Tie input to all       -> "In{i} All"
#     {output}%/$        — View a tie (verbose 2/3 answers "Out{o} In{i} ...")
#     {output}*{s}B      — Video mute an output   -> "Vmt{o}*{s}"
#     {output}*{s}Z      — Audio mute an output   -> "Amt{o}*{s}"
#     {output}B/Z        — View an output's mute state
#     Esc I{n}HDCP<CR>   — Input HDCP/source status -> "HdcpI{n}*{0|1|2}"
#     Front panel pushes: "{oo}Vmt{s}" / "{oo}Amt{s}" / "Qik"
#
#   Bulk views (matrix), one reply for many outputs or inputs, which the poll
#   uses instead of a view per output:
#     Esc 0*{o}*1VC<CR>  — the video ties of 16 outputs from output o
#                          -> "Vgp00*Out{oo} {ii} {ii} ... Vid" (DXP, verbose
#                          2/3; the XTP and CrossPoint guides show no tag)
#     Esc 0*{o}*2VC<CR>  — the same for audio ties -> "... Aud"
#     Esc VM<CR>         — every output's mutes -> "Mut{d}{d}...", one digit
#                          per output: 1 video, 2 audio, 4 analog audio
#     Esc IHDCP<CR>      — every input's HDCP status -> "HdcpI00*{d}{d}..."
#                          (DXP and XTP; an analog CrossPoint has none)
#
#   CAUTION (why matrix polling is roster-gated): the bare view forms ("2!",
#   "2Z", "2B") are ACTIONS in the single-output dialect (select input 2 /
#   mute on), and an unknown Esc command answers an error. The matrix views
#   are only sent while outputs or inputs are configured, so a scaler with
#   the default counts of 0 never receives them.
#
# On connect the driver sets verbose mode 3 (Esc 3CV) so views get tagged
# replies ("Out{o} In{i} ...", "Mut...", "HdcpI00*...").
#
# Power save (DXP HD 4K PLUS guide p. 26 and p. 51): Esc {n}PSAV<CR> answers
# "Psav{n}". Mode 1 ends at any SIS command, a front panel press or a power
# cycle (the DXP guide also lists only Esc 0PSAV, the front panel, PCS and a
# power cycle on p. 51; a DSC 301 HD leaves it only at Esc 0PSAV or a front
# panel press, and has no mode 2 and no verbose mode, so it never answers the
# Vrb3 the reset rule reads), so the poll is held while the switcher reports
# mode 1. Mode 2 answers
# viewing commands and ends only at Esc 0PSAV<CR>, so the poll runs. The view
# Esc PSAV<CR> is documented as answering the bare digit; whether verbose
# mode 3 tags it "Psav{n}" is not verified. A unit without power save answers
# E10, its power_save stays blank, and its poll is never held.
#
# Password (DTP CrossPoint 4K setup guide 68-2368-51 Rev. B pp. 21-22; SW HD
# 4K PLUS user guide 68-2940-01 Rev. E): Extron sets every account's password
# to the unit's serial number at the factory. On port 23 a protected unit
# sends its copyright line, then "\r\nPassword:" with no line ending; the right
# password gets "\r\nLogin Administrator\r\n" (or "Login User"), a wrong one
# gets the prompt again. An unprotected unit asks nothing. Captured on an SW4
# HD 4K PLUS 1.02 (2026-10-28): the wrong-password prompt comes back about 3 s
# later, and a bare CR after the login is ignored.
#
# The platform's telnet_login answers a username prompt and then a password
# prompt; Extron asks for a password only. So the auth block below types the
# password at the first prompt (username_field: password), then waits for the
# line break that opens either answer and sends an empty line, which the
# switcher ignores after a good login. "Login " then confirms it; a refusal
# never says it, so the attempt fails as a refused login after the timeout.
# A blank Password skips the login (an unprotected unit). A protected unit
# with no password entered answers every line with the prompt, which the
# "^Password:$" rule turns into last_error.
#
# SW HD 4K PLUS (presentation switchers, guide p. 28): the Information request
# I answers "In{i} Ausw{m} Afmt{a} Vmt{v}" (selected input, auto-input switch
# mode, embedded audio mute, video mute), read below. While auto-input
# switching is on, a manual input select answers E10 (measured, 1.02).

id: extron_sis
name: Extron SIS Protocol
manufacturer: Extron
category: switcher
version: 1.12.0
author: OpenAVC
# learned_from on the input and output counts.
min_platform_version: "0.37.0"
description: >
  Controls Extron products via the SIS (Simple Instruction Set) protocol.
  Covers crosspoint matrix switchers (DXP, CrossPoint), presentation
  switchers (IN Series), scalers (DSC, DVS), distribution amplifiers,
  and DSP products. On matrix models each configured output and input is
  a child entity with per-output routing and mute state. Works over TCP
  (port 23) or RS-232 (9600 8N1).

source_url: https://www.extron.com/article/sisseries
tags: [matrix-switcher, scaler, distribution-amplifier, sis, generic]
verified: false
simulated: true
protocols: [extron_sis]
ports: [23]
compatible_models:
  - manufacturer: Extron
    models:
      - DXP Series matrix switchers
      - CrossPoint Series matrix switchers
      - IN Series presentation switchers
      - SW HD 4K PLUS Series switchers
      - DSC Series scalers
      - DVS Series scalers
      - DTP Series transmitters and receivers
      - DA Series distribution amplifiers
      - DMP Series DSPs
    confidence: untested
    notes: >
      Any Extron product implementing the SIS protocol (~200 products).
      For matrix switchers, set Input Count / Output Count to the frame
      size to get per-output routing and mute state; leave both 0 for
      single-output devices. Newer Extron units ship with their serial
      number as the password: enter it in Password. Verified on an SW4 HD
      4K PLUS (firmware 1.02): password login, input select, video mute,
      auto-input switching.

transport: tcp
transports: [tcp, serial]
delimiter: "\r\n"

help:
  overview: >
    Universal control for Extron products using the SIS protocol. Works with
    200+ products including crosspoint matrix switchers, presentation switchers,
    scalers, distribution amplifiers, and DSPs. On matrix switchers, configure
    the frame size (Input Count / Output Count) and every output becomes a
    child entity tracking its routed input and mute state, with per-input
    source detection.
  setup: >
    1. Connect the Extron device to the network, or to RS-232 (9600 8N1)
    directly or through a bridge.
    2. For network control, set the device's IP address and use port 23
    (default). A new Extron unit is at 192.168.254.254 with DHCP off; give
    it an address on your network first.
    3. Enter the switcher's password in Password. A new unit's password is
    its serial number, printed on its label. Leave it blank only if the
    switcher has no password.
    4. Matrix switchers (DXP, CrossPoint, XTP): set Input Count and Output
    Count to the frame size (e.g. 8 and 4 for a DXP 84). Each output and
    input becomes a child entity. Leave Output Count at 0 for single-output
    devices (scalers, presentation switchers, DAs); they use the plain
    Select Input / volume / mute commands. On an SW HD 4K PLUS, set Input
    Count to its inputs to see each input's source.
    5. Select Input is refused while Auto-Input Switching is on; set it to
    Off for manual switching.
    6. Extron recommends a 100ms delay between commands (pre-configured).

discovery:
  # Extron telnet (port 23) sends a copyright banner the moment the
  # socket opens (DXP HD 4K PLUS guide, "Copyright Information"):
  #   "(c) Copyright 2014, Extron Electronics, DXP HD 4K PLUS, V1.06"
  # So the probe sends nothing and reads it. It used to send Esc 3CV,
  # which SETS verbose mode 3: a write typed into every port-23 device a
  # scan reached.
  tcp_probe:
    port: 23
    expect_regex: '(?:©|\(c\))[^\n]*?\d{4}[^\n]*?Extron\s+Electronics'
    extract_manufacturer: "Extron"
    extract:
      model:
        regex: '((?:DTP|IN|DXP|SW|MPS|SMP|XTP|SMD|DSP|IPL|MLC|NAV)[A-Za-z0-9 /.+-]+)'
      firmware:
        regex: 'V(\d+\.\d+(?:\.\d+)?)'
  oui:
    - "00:05:a6"

default_config:
  host: ""
  port: 23
  baudrate: 9600
  password: ""
  input_count: 0
  output_count: 0
  poll_interval: 10
  inter_command_delay: 0.1

config_schema:
  host:
    type: string
    required: true
    label: IP Address
  port:
    type: integer
    default: 23
    label: Port
  baudrate:
    type: integer
    default: 9600
    label: Baud Rate (serial)
    description: "Extron RS-232 control runs at 9600 8N1."
  password:
    type: string
    secret: true
    default: ""
    label: Password
    description: >
      The switcher's administrator or user password. A new unit's password
      is its serial number. Leave blank if the switcher has no password.
  input_count:
    type: integer
    default: 0
    min: 0
    label: Input Count
    learned_from: matrix_inputs
    description: >
      Number of inputs on a matrix switcher — each becomes an Input child
      with source-detect state. A matrix reports its size when it connects,
      and it is saved here. On an SW HD 4K PLUS, set it to the switcher's
      inputs to see each one's source. Leave 0 for other single-output
      devices.
  output_count:
    type: integer
    default: 0
    min: 0
    label: Output Count
    learned_from: matrix_outputs
    description: >
      Number of outputs on a matrix switcher. Each becomes an Output child
      tracking its routed input and mute state. A matrix reports its size
      when it connects, and it is saved here. Leave 0 for single-output
      devices (scalers, presentation switchers, DAs).
  poll_interval:
    type: integer
    default: 10
    min: 0
    label: Poll Interval (sec)
  inter_command_delay:
    type: number
    default: 0.1
    label: Inter-Command Delay (sec)
    description: "Extron recommends 100ms between commands"

on_connect:
  - "\x1b3CV\r\n"
  - "\x1bPSAV\r"
  # Firmware: "Ver01*1.02" in verbose mode 3 (SW4 HD 4K PLUS 1.02).
  - "Q"

# The password login, typed at the first prompt (see the header). The second
# "prompt" is the line break that opens the switcher's answer, and the second
# credential is a config field no driver sets, so only the line ending goes:
# a bare CR, which the switcher ignores after a good login. telnet_login
# skips the login while the field it types first (here the password) is
# blank. A refusal is the prompt again, about 3 s later, never "Login ", so
# it fails as a refused login once timeout_seconds pass after that.
auth:
  type: telnet_login
  username_prompt: "Password:"
  username_field: password
  password_prompt: "\r\n"
  password_field: unused_second_line
  success_pattern: "Login "
  line_ending: "\r"
  timeout_seconds: 5

state_variables:
  input:
    type: integer
    label: Current Input
    help: "Single-output devices: the selected input. On a matrix, the last input routed to all outputs."
  matrix_inputs:
    type: integer
    label: Matrix Inputs
    help: "Video inputs the matrix reports (Information request). Blank on a single-output device."
  matrix_outputs:
    type: integer
    label: Matrix Outputs
    help: "Video outputs the matrix reports (Information request). Blank on a single-output device."
  volume:
    type: integer
    label: Volume Level
    help: "Audio output volume on a 0–100 scale (single-output devices)."
  mute:
    type: boolean
    label: Audio Mute
    help: "True when the audio output is muted (single-output devices)."
  video_mute:
    type: boolean
    label: Video Mute
    help: "True when the video output is blanked, with or without its sync (single-output devices; matrix mute-all acks also land here)."
  embedded_audio_mute:
    type: boolean
    label: Embedded Audio Mute
    help: "True when the audio carried on the HDMI output is muted (SW HD 4K PLUS)."
  auto_switch:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 2
    label: Auto-Input Switching
    help: "0 off (manual switching), 1 or 2 an automatic mode (the Auto-Input Switching setting says which input each picks). Select Input is refused while it is not 0 (SW HD 4K PLUS, DSC scalers)."
  last_error:
    type: string
    label: Last Error
    help: "Why the switcher is not answering commands, when it says so."
  firmware:
    type: string
    label: Firmware Version
    help: "Firmware version string reported by the device."
  signal_active:
    type: boolean
    label: Signal Detected
    help: "True when the device detects a valid signal on the active input ('Sig1' / 'Sig0' notification)."
  power_save:
    type: integer
    label: Power Save Mode
    min: 0
    max: 2
    help: "0 normal, 1 low power, 2 low power with the front panel locked. Polling pauses in mode 1. Blank on a unit without power save."

# One frame, two switching planes: video and audio, which can be routed
# together or broken away. Each reports on its own property.
routing:
  destination_child_type: output
  source_child_type: input
  planes:
    - label: Video
      route_property: input
      command: route
    - label: Audio
      route_property: audio_input
      command: route_audio

child_entity_types:
  output:
    label: Output
    label_plural: Outputs
    id_format: { type: integer, min: 1, max: 128 }
    state_variables:
      input:
        type: integer
        label: Routed Input
        help: "Input currently tied to this output for video (0 = untied)."
        cloud_priority: high
      audio_input:
        type: integer
        label: Routed Audio Input
        help: "Input currently tied to this output for audio (0 = untied; follows video on AV ties)."
      video_mute:
        type: boolean
        label: Video Muted
        help: "True when this output's video (and embedded audio) is muted."
        cloud_priority: high
      audio_mute:
        type: boolean
        label: Audio Muted
        help: "True when any of this output's audio paths is muted (models report HDMI/analog/S-PDIF mute combinations; any non-zero state reads as muted)."
    summary_fields: [input, video_mute]
    instances:
      count_from_state: matrix_outputs
      count_from: output_count
      label: "Output {id}"
  input:
    label: Input
    label_plural: Inputs
    id_format: { type: integer, min: 1, max: 128 }
    state_variables:
      signal:
        type: boolean
        label: Source Detected
        help: "True when a source is detected on this input (from the HDCP status query; DXP-class matrices)."
        cloud_priority: high
      hdcp:
        type: enum
        values: ["unknown", "none", "hdcp", "non_hdcp"]
        label: HDCP Status
        help: "HDCP state of the detected source: none = no source, hdcp = HDCP-compliant source, non_hdcp = source without HDCP."
    summary_fields: [signal]
    instances:
      count_from_state: matrix_inputs
      count_from: input_count
      label: "Input {id}"

commands:
  route:
    label: Route Input to Output
    send: "{input}*{output}!"
    help: "Tie an input to an output for video and audio (matrix switchers). Input 0 unties the output."
    params:
      input:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Input Number
        min: 0
        help: "Source input number (0 = untie)"
      output:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Output Number
        min: 1
        help: "Destination output number"

  route_video:
    label: Route Video Only
    send: "{input}*{output}%"
    help: "Tie an input to an output for video only (breakaway; matrix switchers). Input 0 unties."
    params:
      input:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Input Number
        min: 0
      output:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Output Number
        min: 1

  route_audio:
    label: Route Audio Only
    send: "{input}*{output}$"
    help: "Tie an input to an output for audio only (breakaway; matrix switchers). Input 0 unties."
    params:
      input:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Input Number
        min: 0
      output:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Output Number
        min: 1

  route_all:
    label: Route Input to All Outputs
    send: "{input}*!"
    help: "Tie a single input to every output (matrix switchers). Per-output state refreshes on the next poll."
    params:
      input:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Input Number
        min: 1

  select_input:
    label: Select Input
    send: "{input}!"
    help: "Select the active input on a single-output device (scaler, presentation switcher). Refused while Auto-Input Switching is on. On DXP-class matrices this form views an output's tie instead — use Route there."
    params:
      input:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Input Number
        min: 1

  set_volume:
    label: Set Volume
    send: "{level}V"
    help: "Set the audio volume level on a presentation switcher with a volume control, such as the IN Series. The SW HD 4K PLUS and DSC scalers have none."
    params:
      level:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Volume Level
        min: 0
        max: 100
        help: "Volume level 0-100"

  mute_on:
    label: Mute Audio
    send: "1Z"
    help: "Mute the audio output (single-output devices; on a matrix use Output Audio Mute)."

  mute_off:
    label: Unmute Audio
    send: "0Z"
    help: "Unmute the audio output (single-output devices)."

  video_mute_on:
    label: Video Mute On
    send: "1B"
    help: "Blank the video output (single-output devices; on a matrix use Output Video Mute)."

  video_mute_off:
    label: Video Mute Off
    send: "0B"
    help: "Restore the video output (single-output devices)."

  # 2B: video and sync mute (SW HD 4K PLUS guide; "Vmt2" on an SW4 1.02).
  video_sync_mute_on:
    label: Video and Sync Mute On
    send: "2B"
    help: "Blank the video output and stop its sync, so the display shows no signal (single-output devices; on a matrix use Output Video and Sync Mute). Video Mute Off restores it."

  embedded_audio_mute_on:
    label: Embedded Audio Mute On
    send: "\x1b1AFMT\r"
    help: "Mute the audio carried on the HDMI output (SW HD 4K PLUS)."

  embedded_audio_mute_off:
    label: Embedded Audio Mute Off
    send: "\x1b0AFMT\r"
    help: "Unmute the audio carried on the HDMI output (SW HD 4K PLUS)."

  output_video_mute_on:
    label: Output Video Mute On
    send: "{output}*1B"
    help: "Mute an output's video and embedded audio (matrix switchers)."
    params:
      output:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Output Number
        min: 1

  output_video_mute_off:
    label: Output Video Mute Off
    send: "{output}*0B"
    help: "Unmute an output's video (matrix switchers)."
    params:
      output:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Output Number
        min: 1

  # {o}*2B: video and sync mute (DTP CrossPoint 4K setup guide p. 24).
  output_video_sync_mute_on:
    label: Output Video and Sync Mute On
    send: "{output}*2B"
    help: "Mute an output's video and stop its sync, so the display shows no signal (DXP; the XTP CrossPoint and CrossPoint 450 have video mute only). Output Video Mute Off restores it."
    params:
      output:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Output Number
        min: 1

  output_audio_mute_on:
    label: Output Audio Mute On
    send: "{output}*1Z"
    help: "Mute an output's audio (matrix switchers). Models with multiple audio paths treat value 1 as the HDMI/primary path — deeper mute combinations are model-specific."
    params:
      output:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Output Number
        min: 1

  output_audio_mute_off:
    label: Output Audio Mute Off
    send: "{output}*0Z"
    help: "Unmute an output's audio (matrix switchers)."
    params:
      output:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Output Number
        min: 1

  # Global presets: {n}. recalls, {n}, saves ("Rpr{n}" / "Spr{n}"; DXP guide,
  # CrossPoint 450 Plus guide "9," -> "Spr09"). On an XTP CrossPoint those forms
  # are analog input presets; its global presets are the PRST commands below.
  recall_preset:
    label: Recall Preset
    send: "{preset}."
    help: "Recall a saved routing preset (DXP, CrossPoint; on an XTP CrossPoint use Recall Preset (XTP)). The valid preset range is model-specific (e.g. 16 global presets on DXP HD 4K PLUS; more on larger frames) — the device rejects an invalid number."
    params:
      preset:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Preset Number
        min: 1

  save_preset:
    label: Save Preset
    send: "{preset},"
    help: "Save the current routing configuration to a preset (DXP, CrossPoint; on an XTP CrossPoint use Save Preset (XTP)). The valid preset range is model-specific."
    params:
      preset:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Preset Number
        min: 1

  # XTP CrossPoint global presets (XTP guide): Esc R{n}PRST<CR> -> "PrstR{nn}",
  # Esc S{n}PRST<CR> -> "PrstS{nn}".
  recall_preset_xtp:
    label: Recall Preset (XTP)
    send: "\x1bR{preset}PRST\r"
    help: "Recall a saved global preset on an XTP CrossPoint. The switcher refuses one that was never saved."
    params:
      preset:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Preset Number
        min: 1

  save_preset_xtp:
    label: Save Preset (XTP)
    send: "\x1bS{preset}PRST\r"
    help: "Save the current ties to a global preset on an XTP CrossPoint."
    params:
      preset:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Preset Number
        min: 1

  power_save_off:
    label: Power Save Off
    send: "\x1b0PSAV\r"
    sets: { power_save: 0 }
    help: "Returns the switcher to normal operation and resumes polling."

  power_save_1:
    label: Power Save Mode 1
    send: "\x1b1PSAV\r"
    sets: { power_save: 1 }
    help: "Low power: everything but control stops and the fans slow. Polling pauses until Power Save Off is sent. On a DXP a front panel press or any other command also ends this mode (a DSC scaler leaves it only at Power Save Off or a front panel press), but polling stays paused until Power Save Off, or until the switcher reconnects after a power cycle. While polling is paused, nothing notices the switcher going offline."

  power_save_2:
    label: Power Save Mode 2
    send: "\x1b2PSAV\r"
    sets: { power_save: 2 }
    help: "Low power with the front panel locked: everything but control stops, and ties, mutes and presets are refused until Power Save Off is sent. Polling continues."

# Quick actions — routing and preset recall are the everyday matrix moves;
# audio mute covers the single-output devices.
actions:
  - id: route
    icon: shuffle
  - id: route_all
    icon: fast-forward
  - id: recall_preset
    icon: bookmark
  - id: mute_on
    icon: volume-x
  - id: mute_off
    icon: volume-2

# Auto-input switching (SW HD 4K PLUS guide p. 23): Esc {m}AUSW<CR> answers
# "Ausw{m}"; the polled I reports the mode. While it is not 0 a manual input
# select is refused. A unit without the mode answers E10 and the setting stays
# blank.
device_settings:
  auto_switch:
    type: enum
    label: Auto-Input Switching
    help: "Off for manual switching; Select Input is refused in the other two modes. Mode 1: on an SW HD 4K PLUS the priority order set on the switcher (else the highest active input), on a DSC scaler the highest input. Mode 2: on an SW HD 4K PLUS the most recently connected input, on a DSC scaler the lowest input."
    state_key: auto_switch
    default: 0
    setup: false
    values:
      - { value: "0", label: "Off (manual switching)" }
      - { value: "1", label: "Mode 1" }
      - { value: "2", label: "Mode 2" }
    write:
      send: "\x1b{value}AUSW\r"

responses:
  # ── Matrix tie acks / verbose view-tie responses ──
  # "Out2 In1 All" (AV tie), "Out2 In1 Vid" (video breakaway),
  # "Out2 In1 Aud" (audio breakaway). These must come before the flat
  # In-rule: the old unanchored 'In(\d+) All' matched INSIDE the tie ack
  # and stored the input while discarding the output number.
  - match: '^Out(\d+) In(\d+) All$'
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: "$1", state: { input: "$2", audio_input: "$2" } }
  # "RGB": the XTP CrossPoint and CrossPoint 450 answer an & tie (video only,
  # the same as %) with "Out04 In10 RGB".
  - match: '^Out(\d+) In(\d+) (?:Vid|RGB)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: "$1", state: { input: "$2" } }
  - match: '^Out(\d+) In(\d+) Aud$'
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: "$1", state: { audio_input: "$2" } }

  # Input select / input-to-all ack: "In1 All" (also "In1 Vid"/"In1 Aud"
  # from breakaway-to-all forms). Single-output devices report their
  # selected input here.
  - match: '^In(\d+) (?:All|Vid|Aud|RGB)$'
    set: { input: "$1" }

  # The SW HD 4K PLUS answer to the polled Information request I (guide
  # p. 28; "In1 Ausw0 Afmt0 Vmt0" on an SW4 1.02): the selected input, the
  # auto-input switch mode, embedded audio mute and video mute (2 = video and
  # sync).
  - match: '^In(\d+) Ausw([0-2]) Afmt([01]) Vmt([0-2])$'
    set: { input: "$1", auto_switch: "$2" }
    mappings:
      - state: embedded_audio_mute
        group: 3
        type: boolean
        map: { "1": true, "0": false }
      - state: video_mute
        group: 4
        type: boolean
        map: { "2": true, "1": true, "0": false }
  # The DSC 301 HD answer to I (guide, Information Requests): "Vid{i} Typ{t} Std{s} Blk{m}
  # Hrt{h} Vrt{v}", input and video mute (Blk 1 = to black, 2 = video and
  # sync). The DSC has no verbose mode, so it is never tagged.
  - match: '^Vid(\d+) Typ\S+ Std\S+ Blk([0-2]) Hrt\S+ Vrt\S+$'
    set: { input: "$1" }
    mappings:
      - state: video_mute
        group: 2
        type: boolean
        map: { "2": true, "1": true, "0": false }
  - match: '^Afmt([01])$'
    mappings:
      - state: embedded_audio_mute
        group: 1
        type: boolean
        map: { "1": true, "0": false }
  - match: '^Ausw([0-2])$'
    set: { auto_switch: "$1" }

  # A protected switcher with no Password entered answers every line with
  # the prompt (the login was skipped). The prompt has no line ending of its
  # own; the next one's leading CR LF frames it.
  - match: '^Password:$'
    set: { last_error: "The switcher asks for a password. Enter it in this device's Password setting." }

  # ── Per-output mute acks / views (matrix): "Vmt2*1", "Amt2*3" ──
  # 2 = video and sync mute (DXP guide; DTP CrossPoint 4K guides).
  - match: '^Vmt(\d+)\*([0-2])$'
    child_set:
      - type: output
        id: "$1"
        state:
          video_mute: { group: 2, map: { "2": "true", "1": "true", "0": "false" } }
  - match: '^Amt(\d+)\*0$'
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: "$1", state: { audio_mute: "false" } }
  # Audio mute values 1-7 are model-specific path combinations (HDMI,
  # analog, S/PDIF) — any non-zero state reads as muted.
  - match: '^Amt(\d+)\*[1-7]$'
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: "$1", state: { audio_mute: "true" } }

  # Front-panel push notifications (matrix): "02Vmt1" / "02Amt0"
  - match: '^(\d+)Vmt([0-2])$'
    child_set:
      - type: output
        id: "$1"
        state:
          video_mute: { group: 2, map: { "2": "true", "1": "true", "0": "false" } }
  - match: '^(\d+)Amt([01])$'
    child_set:
      - type: output
        id: "$1"
        state:
          audio_mute: { group: 2, map: { "1": "true", "0": "false" } }

  # Flat mute acks (single-output devices; a matrix mute-all ack "Vmt1"
  # also lands here). Flat set: takes $N refs or statics only, so the
  # on/off values are split into static rules.
  - match: '^Amt1$'
    set: { mute: "true" }
  - match: '^Amt0$'
    set: { mute: "false" }
  # Vmt2: video and sync mute ("Vmt2" from 2B on an SW4 1.02).
  - match: '^Vmt[12]$'
    set: { video_mute: "true" }
  - match: '^Vmt0$'
    set: { video_mute: "false" }

  # ── Bulk views (matrix): one reply covers many outputs or inputs ──
  # Ties, 16 outputs a read from the output asked for (Esc 0*{o}*1VC video,
  # *2VC audio; preset 0 means the current ties): DXP guide "Global Presets",
  # XTP CrossPoint guide p. 113, CrossPoint 450 Plus/Ultra guide p. 100. Each
  # place is a two-digit input (00 = untied), "--" where the frame has no
  # output. The DXP tags the reply in verbose mode 2/3 with the page's first
  # output ("Vgp00*Out17 ..."), which says where the list starts.
  - match: '^Vgp\d+\*Out(\d+) ((?:(?:\d\d|--) ?)+)Vid$'
    child_list: { type: output, group: $2, element: '(\d\d)|--', start: $1, state: { input: $1 } }
  - match: '^Vgp\d+\*Out(\d+) ((?:(?:\d\d|--) ?)+)Aud$'
    child_list: { type: output, group: $2, element: '(\d\d)|--', start: $1, state: { audio_input: $1 } }
  # The XTP and CrossPoint guides show the reply without that tag. Untagged,
  # a reply could be any page, so it is read only while the matrix reports 16
  # outputs or fewer, where the one page starts at output 1. (A larger XTP or
  # CrossPoint frame that does not tag the reply keeps its last ties until a
  # tie is made: unverified on hardware.)
  - match: '^((?:(?:\d\d|--) ?)+)Vid$'
    only_when: { key: matrix_outputs, operator: lte, value: 16 }
    child_list: { type: output, element: '(\d\d)|--', state: { input: $1 } }
  - match: '^((?:(?:\d\d|--) ?)+)Aud$'
    only_when: { key: matrix_outputs, operator: lte, value: 16 }
    child_list: { type: output, element: '(\d\d)|--', state: { audio_input: $1 } }

  # Every output's mutes, one digit per output from output 1 (Esc VM, "Mut"
  # in verbose mode 2/3; same three guides). The digit adds 1 for video, 2 for
  # (digital) audio and 4 for analog audio: the XTP reports 0-7, the DXP and
  # CrossPoint 0-3. Any audio path muted reads as muted.
  - match: '^Mut ?([0-7 ]+)$'
    child_list:
      type: output
      element: '([0-7])'
      state:
        video_mute: { group: 1, map: { "0": "false", "1": "true", "2": "false", "3": "true", "4": "false", "5": "true", "6": "false", "7": "true" } }
        audio_mute: { group: 1, map: { "0": "false", "1": "false", "2": "true", "3": "true", "4": "true", "5": "true", "6": "true", "7": "true" } }

  # Every input's HDCP status, one digit per input from input 1 (Esc IHDCP,
  # tagged "HdcpI00*" in verbose mode 2/3; DXP guide p. 43, XTP guide). Ahead
  # of the per-input rules below, which would read a one-input list as input 0.
  - match: '^HdcpI00\*([0-2 ]+)$'
    child_list:
      type: input
      element: '([0-2])'
      state:
        signal: { group: 1, map: { "0": "false", "1": "true", "2": "true" } }
        hdcp: { group: 1, map: { "0": "none", "1": "hdcp", "2": "non_hdcp" } }
  # The SW HD 4K PLUS tags the same list "HdcpI" with nothing after it and
  # ends it with a space ("HdcpI0 0 0 0 " on an SW4 1.02, guide p. 25).
  - match: '^HdcpI([0-2](?: [0-2])*) ?$'
    child_list:
      type: input
      element: '([0-2])'
      state:
        signal: { group: 1, map: { "0": "false", "1": "true", "2": "true" } }
        hdcp: { group: 1, map: { "0": "none", "1": "hdcp", "2": "non_hdcp" } }

  # ── Per-input source/HDCP status (matrix): "HdcpI3*1" ──
  # 0 = no source detected, 1 = HDCP source, 2 = non-HDCP source.
  - match: '^HdcpI(\d+)\*0$'
    child_set:
      - { type: input, id: "$1", state: { signal: "false", hdcp: "none" } }
  - match: '^HdcpI(\d+)\*1$'
    child_set:
      - { type: input, id: "$1", state: { signal: "true", hdcp: "hdcp" } }
  - match: '^HdcpI(\d+)\*2$'
    child_set:
      - { type: input, id: "$1", state: { signal: "true", hdcp: "non_hdcp" } }

  # Volume response: "Vol50" or "Ds50"
  - match: '^Vol(\d+)$'
    set: { volume: "$1" }
  - match: '^Ds(\d+)$'
    set: { volume: "$1" }

  # Firmware, the answer to Q at connect: "Ver01*1.02" in verbose mode 3
  # (SW4 HD 4K PLUS 1.02).
  - match: '^Ver\d+\*(\S+)$'
    set: { firmware: "$1" }
  # Firmware: "Ver1.02.0001" (legacy unanchored — format varies by family)
  - match: 'Ver(\S+)'
    set: { firmware: "$1" }

  # Power save: "Psav1", the answer to Esc 1PSAV (and, if verbose mode 3
  # tags it, to the view Esc PSAV).
  - match: '^Psav([0-2])$'
    set: { power_save: "$1" }
  # The answer to the verbose-mode command sent on every connect. Any SIS
  # command ends mode 1, so a switcher last read in mode 1 has left it: a
  # power cycle, or a reconnect, resumes polling.
  - match: '^Vrb3$'
    only_when: { key: power_save, operator: eq, value: 1 }
    set: { power_save: 0 }

  # Signal status (SW HD 4K PLUS guide p. 24, "Sig0 0 0 0*0" on an SW4 1.02):
  # one digit per input, then "*" and the output's. The output's is the
  # active input's signal. Anchored: unanchored "Sig0" matched inside a list
  # whose active input had a signal ("Sig0 1 0 0*1").
  - match: '^Sig[01](?: [01])*\*([01])$'
    mappings:
      - state: signal_active
        group: 1
        type: boolean
        map: { "1": true, "0": false }
  - match: '^Sig1$'
    set: { signal_active: true }
  - match: '^Sig0$'
    set: { signal_active: false }

  # Preset acknowledgements, read so a recall or save is not an unread reply:
  # "Rpr05" / "Spr09" (DXP, CrossPoint; Rpr also when a preset is recalled at
  # the front panel), "PrstR05" / "PrstS08" (XTP).
  - match: '^(?:Rpr|Spr|PrstR|PrstS)\d+$'
    set: {}

  # Matrix size, the reply to the polled Information request "I"
  # (DXP HD 4K PLUS guide, "General information"): "V8X4 A8X2", prefixed
  # "Info00*" in verbose mode 2/3. The V half is the video matrix
  # (inputs X outputs); the A half counts analog/S-PDIF audio outputs, not
  # the matrix, so it is ignored. Matched only for two or more outputs: a
  # single-output device stays on the flat surface this driver uses for it
  # (a scaler's I is signal information, "Vid1 Typ6 ...", and never matches).
  - match: '^(?:Info\d*\*)?V(\d+)X([2-9]|[1-9]\d+) A\d+X\d+$'
    set: { matrix_inputs: "$1", matrix_outputs: "$2" }

polling:
  # Any SIS command ends power save mode 1, so the poll waits it out.
  when_state: { power_save: [0, 2] }
  queries:
    # Single-output dialect (matrices answer these with info strings or
    # errors, which is benign — their state rides the per-output queries).
    # query_for names the state variable each terse query reports; the
    # letters say nothing about what comes back, so the pairing is declared.
    - { send: "I", query_for: input }
    - { send: "V", query_for: volume }
    - { send: "Z", query_for: mute }
    # Matrix dialect, only sent while outputs or inputs are configured: the
    # bulk views, a page of 16 outputs per tie read (once for a frame of up
    # to 16 outputs, from outputs 1, 17, 33 ... on a larger one), and one
    # read for every output's mutes and one for every input's HDCP status.
    # query_for names what each reports, so the simulator answers it from
    # every output's or input's own modeled state.
    - { each_child: output, page_size: 16, send: "\x1b0*{child_id}*1VC\r", query_for: input }
    - { each_child: output, page_size: 16, send: "\x1b0*{child_id}*2VC\r", query_for: audio_input }
    - { send: "\x1bVM\r", query_for: output.video_mute, when: output_count }
    - { send: "\x1bIHDCP\r", query_for: input.hdcp, when: input_count }

# ── SIMULATOR DEFINITION ──
# Models an 8x4 DXP-style matrix in verbose mode 3 (tagged responses), with
# the single-output dialect's volume kept so the flat commands round-trip.
# Per-output/per-input state uses the child model's dotted keys. Seeding
# them here also rosters the 4 outputs and 8 inputs, so the bulk views
# (declared with query_for above) answer from each child's own state; only
# the mute view needs a handler.
simulator:
  push_state: true
  initial_state:
    input: 1
    volume: 50
    mute: false
    video_mute: false
    embedded_audio_mute: false
    auto_switch: 0
    firmware: "1.04"
    signal_active: true
    power_save: 0
    output.1.input: 1
    output.2.input: 1
    output.3.input: 1
    output.4.input: 1
    output.1.audio_input: 1
    output.2.audio_input: 1
    output.3.audio_input: 1
    output.4.audio_input: 1
    output.1.video_mute: false
    output.2.video_mute: false
    output.3.video_mute: false
    output.4.video_mute: false
    output.1.audio_mute: false
    output.2.audio_mute: false
    output.3.audio_mute: false
    output.4.audio_mute: false
    input.1.signal: true
    input.1.hdcp: hdcp
    input.2.signal: true
    input.2.hdcp: hdcp
    input.3.signal: true
    input.3.hdcp: non_hdcp
    input.4.signal: false
    input.4.hdcp: none
    input.5.signal: false
    input.5.hdcp: none
    input.6.signal: false
    input.6.hdcp: none
    input.7.signal: false
    input.7.hdcp: none
    input.8.signal: false
    input.8.hdcp: none

  delays:
    command_response: 0.02   # 20ms — realistic for Extron SIS over TCP

  controls:
    - type: matrix
      label: Video Routing
      inputs: 8
      outputs: 4
      state_pattern: "output.{output}.input"
    - type: slider
      key: volume
      label: Volume
      min: 0
      max: 100
    - type: toggle
      key: mute
      label: Audio Mute
    - type: indicator
      key: signal_active
      label: Signal
      color_map:
        "true": "#22c55e"
        "false": "#6b7089"
    - type: indicator
      key: firmware
      label: Firmware

  notifications:
    input:
      '*': 'In{value} All'
    volume:
      '*': 'Vol{value}'
    mute:
      'true': 'Amt1'
      'false': 'Amt0'

  command_handlers:
    # Verbose mode select: Esc 3CV
    - match: '\x1b3CV.*'
      handler: |
        respond("Vrb3\r\n")

    # Power save: Esc {n}PSAV  ->  "Psav{n}"; the view Esc PSAV answers the
    # bare digit, as the guide's table shows it.
    - match: '\x1b([0-2])PSAV.*'
      handler: |
        state["power_save"] = int(match.group(1))
        respond("Psav" + match.group(1) + "\r\n")
    - match: '\x1bPSAV.*'
      handler: |
        respond(str(state.get("power_save", 0)) + "\r\n")

    # AV tie: {input}*{output}!  ->  "Out{o} In{i} All"
    - match: '(\d+)\*(\d+)!'
      handler: |
        inp = int(match.group(1))
        out = int(match.group(2))
        if f"output.{out}.input" in state:
            state[f"output.{out}.input"] = inp
            state[f"output.{out}.audio_input"] = inp
            respond(f"Out{out} In{inp} All\r\n")
        else:
            respond("E01\r\n")

    # Video-only tie: {input}*{output}% (or &)
    - match: '(\d+)\*(\d+)[%&]'
      handler: |
        inp = int(match.group(1))
        out = int(match.group(2))
        if f"output.{out}.input" in state:
            state[f"output.{out}.input"] = inp
            respond(f"Out{out} In{inp} Vid\r\n")
        else:
            respond("E01\r\n")

    # Audio-only tie: {input}*{output}$
    - match: '(\d+)\*(\d+)\$'
      handler: |
        inp = int(match.group(1))
        out = int(match.group(2))
        if f"output.{out}.audio_input" in state:
            state[f"output.{out}.audio_input"] = inp
            respond(f"Out{out} In{inp} Aud\r\n")
        else:
            respond("E01\r\n")

    # Input to all outputs: {input}*!  ->  "In{i} All"
    - match: '(\d+)\*!'
      handler: |
        inp = int(match.group(1))
        state["input"] = inp
        for i in range(1, 5):
            state[f"output.{i}.input"] = inp
            state[f"output.{i}.audio_input"] = inp
        respond(f"In{inp} All\r\n")

    # Per-output video mute set: {output}*{0|1|2}B  ->  "Vmt{o}*{s}"
    # (2 = video and sync mute)
    - match: '(\d+)\*([0-2])B'
      handler: |
        out = int(match.group(1))
        val = int(match.group(2))
        if f"output.{out}.video_mute" in state:
            state[f"output.{out}.video_mute"] = val != 0
            respond(f"Vmt{out}*{val}\r\n")
        else:
            respond("E01\r\n")

    # Flat video mute (single-output dialect): {0|1|2}B  ->  "Vmt{s}"
    - match: '([0-2])B'
      handler: |
        val = int(match.group(1))
        state["video_mute"] = val != 0
        respond(f"Vmt{val}\r\n")

    # Embedded audio mute: Esc {0|1}AFMT  ->  "Afmt{s}" (SW HD 4K PLUS)
    - match: '\x1b([01])AFMT.*'
      handler: |
        val = int(match.group(1))
        state["embedded_audio_mute"] = val == 1
        respond(f"Afmt{val}\r\n")

    # Auto-input switching: Esc {m}AUSW  ->  "Ausw{m}" (SW HD 4K PLUS)
    - match: '\x1b([0-2])AUSW.*'
      handler: |
        state["auto_switch"] = int(match.group(1))
        respond("Ausw" + match.group(1) + "\r\n")

    # Per-output audio mute set: {output}*{0-7}Z  ->  "Amt{o}*{s}"
    # (values 1-7 are model-specific path combinations; any non-zero
    # state reads as muted, and the ack echoes the exact value)
    - match: '(\d+)\*([0-7])Z'
      handler: |
        out = int(match.group(1))
        val = int(match.group(2))
        if f"output.{out}.audio_mute" in state:
            state[f"output.{out}.audio_mute"] = val != 0
            respond(f"Amt{out}*{val}\r\n")
        else:
            respond("E01\r\n")

    # The bulk tie and HDCP views need no handlers: the polling entries
    # declare query_for, so the simulator answers them from every output's
    # and input's own modeled state, in the shape of the driver's rules.

    # Every output's mutes: one digit per output, 1 for video plus 2 for
    # audio. A handler, because one digit carries two of an output's values.
    - match: '\x1bVM'
      handler: |
        outs = int(config.get("output_count") or 0)
        digits = ""
        for out in range(1, outs + 1):
            video = 1 if state.get(f"output.{out}.video_mute") else 0
            audio = 2 if state.get(f"output.{out}.audio_mute") else 0
            digits += str(video + audio)
        respond(f"Mut{digits}\r\n")

    # View AV tie — on DXP-class units a bare "{output}!" is a view,
    # NOT input-to-all (that form is "{input}*!"). Not polled, so it
    # keeps an explicit handler.
    - match: '(\d+)!'
      handler: |
        out = int(match.group(1))
        if f"output.{out}.input" in state:
            respond(f"Out{out} In{state[f'output.{out}.input']} All\r\n")
        else:
            respond("E01\r\n")

    # Volume set: {level}V (single-output dialect, kept for the flat surface)
    - match: '(\d+)V'
      handler: |
        level = int(match.group(1))
        state["volume"] = max(0, min(100, level))
        respond(f"Vol{state['volume']}\r\n")

    # Query volume
    - match: 'V'
      handler: |
        respond(f"Vol{state['volume']}\r\n")

    # Query flat mute status (bare Z is the status view; SIS has no toggle
    # verb — set mute with 1Z/0Z on single-output devices)
    - match: 'Z'
      handler: |
        val = "1" if state["mute"] else "0"
        respond(f"Amt{val}\r\n")

    # Information query. A matrix answers with its size, the one the
    # project's counts describe (verbose mode 3 adds the Info00* tag; the A
    # half is the DXP's two analog/S-PDIF audio outputs). A single-output
    # device answers as an SW HD 4K PLUS does: input, auto-input switch mode,
    # embedded audio mute, video mute.
    - match: 'I'
      handler: |
        ins = int(config.get("input_count") or 0)
        outs = int(config.get("output_count") or 0)
        if outs > 0:
            respond(f"Info00*V{ins}X{outs} A{ins}X2\r\n")
        else:
            afmt = 1 if state.get("embedded_audio_mute") else 0
            vmt = 1 if state.get("video_mute") else 0
            respond(f"In{state['input']} Ausw{int(state.get('auto_switch') or 0)} Afmt{afmt} Vmt{vmt}\r\n")

    # Firmware query, as verbose mode 3 tags it
    - receive: 'Q'
      respond: "Ver01*{state.firmware}\r\n"

    # Model name
    - receive: "N"
      respond: "SIS 1616\r\n"

    # Firmware query
    - receive: '\*Q'
      respond: "Ver{state.firmware}\r\n"

    # Preset recall/save
    - receive: '(\d+)\.'
      respond: "Rpr{1}\r\n"
    - receive: '(\d+),'
      respond: "Spr{1}\r\n"
    # XTP CrossPoint global presets
    - receive: '\x1bR(\d+)PRST.*'
      respond: "PrstR{1}\r\n"
    - receive: '\x1bS(\d+)PRST.*'
      respond: "PrstS{1}\r\n"

  error_modes:
    communication_timeout:
      description: "Device stops responding to commands"
      behavior: no_response
    garbled_response:
      description: "Corrupted serial data on the wire"
      behavior: corrupt_response
